{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-diagonal-unramified-morphism}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-locally-finite-presentation}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-locally-finite-type}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-open-immersion}", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ ", "SPACE_0003": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:325ee41a408af3554eb256d2edf6f6ad3b17e57090f59ac6d0bfadeebbe0961e", "source_text": "A morphism is unramified (resp.<SPACE_0001>G-unramified) if and only if it is\nlocally of finite type (resp.<SPACE_0002>finite presentation)\nand its diagonal morphism is an open immersion (see\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>).\nWe have seen already that being locally of finite type\n(resp.<SPACE_0003>locally of finite presentation) and an open immersion is\nfpqc local on the base (Lemmas\n<REF_0002>,\n<REF_0003>, and\n<REF_0004>).\nHence the result follows formally.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:719c70b68700b4d3689b7301339566e6becd878b1931a80fc23e0006b9f54556", "unit_id": "tag:02VM:proof"}
