{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$H_1$", "MATH_0002": "$H_1$", "MATH_0003": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0004": "$I \\subset A$", "MATH_0005": "$IB$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Spec(B)$", "MATH_0007": "$H_1$", "MATH_0008": "$B$", "MATH_0009": "$I \\subset A$", "MATH_0010": "$\\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0011": "$H_1$", "MATH_0012": "$A$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties-morphisms}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{divisors-definition-regular-immersion}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{divisors-lemma-flat-base-change-regular-immersion}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties-morphisms}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{more-algebra-lemma-flat-descent-regular-ideal}", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ ", "SPACE_0003": "\\ ", "SPACE_0004": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f8d307d7db987992baa3448e9d5c94ade113dcdd5cbdd4caf5be4b26426718f7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b6a979ac9fcb706428c396b01d8114ae5a7b4cba81a544d054a9d1853df49bbf", "source_text": "We will use the criterion of\nLemma <REF_0001>\nto prove this. By\nDivisors, Definition <REF_0002>\nbeing a Koszul-regular (resp.<SPACE_0001><MATH_0001>-regular, quasi-regular)\nimmersion is Zariski local on the base. By\nDivisors, Lemma <REF_0003>\nbeing a Koszul-regular (resp.<SPACE_0002><MATH_0002>-regular, quasi-regular)\nimmersion is preserved under flat base change.\nThe final hypothesis (3) of\nLemma <REF_0004>\ntranslates into the following algebra statement:\nLet <MATH_0003> be a faithfully flat ring map. Let <MATH_0004> be an ideal.\nIf <MATH_0005> is locally on <MATH_0006> generated by a Koszul-regular\n(resp.<SPACE_0003><MATH_0007>-regular, quasi-regular) sequence in <MATH_0008>, then <MATH_0009>\nis locally on <MATH_0010> generated by a Koszul-regular\n(resp.<SPACE_0004><MATH_0011>-regular, quasi-regular) sequence in <MATH_0012>. This is\nMore on Algebra, Lemma <REF_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:554ad02c684f90a5c6512a16b0d1ab4a35289d94ae4d82796cd2251032223e9b", "unit_id": "tag:0694:proof"}
